{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bluebox MCP server",
    "_postman_id": "6c3f8a2e-4b1d-4f7a-9e5c-2d8b7a1f0c34",
    "description": "Requests for the [Bluebox MCP server](https://docs.bluebox.ai/mcp-server) at `https://app.bluebox.ai/v1/mcp`: JSON-RPC over Streamable HTTP.\n\n**Sign in with OAuth**\n\n1. Send **Setup \u2192 Register the Postman client** first. It saves `client_id`, which **Get New Access Token** needs: without it, sign-in fails with \"Cannot sign in: The app that sent you here is not registered or has been disabled.\" A registration that never gets a token is deleted after 30 days; if sign-in shows that message later, send Register again.\n2. On the collection's **Authorization** tab, select **Get New Access Token** and sign in to Bluebox in the window that opens.\n3. Send the requests in **MCP**.\n\n**Use an access token**\n\nWhere a browser can't open, [create an access token](https://docs.bluebox.ai/mcp-server#create-an-access-token) and set it as `access_token` in a Postman environment, as the **current value** only. Postman syncs and exports initial values, so never put the token there. When `access_token` is set, every request sends it as a bearer token instead of the OAuth token.\n\n**Variables**\n\nCalls without `workspace_id` use your default workspace. `list_workspaces` fills `workspace_id` when it is empty. When you change `workspace_id`, in the collection or in an environment, the other IDs are cleared, because they belong to one workspace.\n\n- `entity_id` scopes `ask` and `repository_id` filters `list_investigations`. Neither is filled for you: `list_services` and `list_repositories` log the IDs to the Postman console, and you copy the one you mean.\n- `list_investigations` saves the newest `investigation_id` and logs which one it is.\n- `ask` saves `conversation_id`.\n\nEmpty variables are left out of tool calls. Requests that need `conversation_id` or `investigation_id` are skipped while it is empty, so a follow-up never starts a new metered run by accident.\n\n`ask` starts a Bluebox run that counts against the workspace's AI usage. Every other tool only reads.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
